<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sabr ad-Din III</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 1415–<a href="/years/1422">1422</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sabr ad-Din III was a prince of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/walashma-dynasty">Walashma dynasty</a> who founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adal-sultanate">Adal Sultanate</a> in about 1415. He returned from exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a> after the defeat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ifat-sultanate">Ifat Sultanate</a> and the execution of its ruler, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saad-ad-din-ii">Sa'ad ad-Din II</a>, by Ethiopian forces. Accounts of the Adal Sultanate credit him with reconstituting Muslim political power in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/horn-of-africa">Horn of Africa</a> in the form of the new sultanate.</p></div>
